<p>…You <em>did</em> ask 028's original author before posting this, right?</p>
<p>So, the underlying horror here is supposed to be that the guy learns something horrible from 028, but forgets it before he can do anything more than hint at a future disaster. Thing is, SCP-028's revelations are permanent, and complete. The subject gains and <em>retains</em> total knowledge of… whatever. You <em>don't</em> forget them a few seconds later. Flawed concept is flawed, rendering the horror hook impossible. Fail.</p>
<p>Downvoted.</p>
<p>If I could remove edcrab's upvote, I would. Poorly written articles happen, but articles that misunderstand the actual premise behind the SCP they reference are <em>unforgiveable</em>.</p>

